                <pb facs="0421" n="333" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg333"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr.
                            Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July 29,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis states that Mr. Griscom reports that the crew of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Knight Commander</hi> testify that the vessel was sunk
                    for want of coal to proceed to Vladivostok, and that the United States
                    Government considers that the sinking of the vessel was not justified by the
                    bare fact that there was contraband of war aboard. Cites as authorities Note to
                    Dana’s Wheaton, eighth edition, page 485, and Hall, Twiss, and Lawrence.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
